// # hw/audio/ANCHOR.oo — Audio HAL Stub (v4.6.0)
//
// Logline: Hardware stub for the AudioCap substrate token. Provides
//          OoAudioBuf type + oo_audio_init/capture/release entry
//          points, all cap-gated via oo_cap_require_audio. On this
//          host (no ALSA lib installed), the stub returns
//          OoResS{ok=0, val="audio_capture: no device"} — proving the
//          cap path works without requiring real hardware. Opt-in
//          `-DUSE_ALSA` enables the real ALSA backend (requires
//          alsa-lib-devel on the host).
//
// Setup:  Pure structural file. The 1 file in this tactical subdir
//         (hw/audio/oo_audio_capture.c) is included by the umbrella
//         oodar.c. The audio.h header is included by oodar.h so
//         external consumers see the type + the 3 entry points. The
//         pattern follows hw/gpu/ANCHOR.oo (HIP shim + OoGpuDevice
//         type) — hardware HALs are part of the substrate role per
//         NORTHSTAR §1.2.
//
// Beats:
//   1. OoAudioBuf type — hw/audio/audio.h
//   2. Lifecycle (init/capture/release) — hw/audio/oo_audio_capture.c
//   3. Cap-gating — every entry point runs oo_cap_require_audio,
//                    which is dual-checked (bitmask + OCap bridge,
//                    v4.5.0).
